      "text": "### 1. Publication Background, Awards/Nominations, and Genre Positioning\n**Title:** The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle  \n**Author:** Stuart Turton  \n**Year of Publication:** 2018  \n**Publisher:** Sourcebooks Landmark  \n**ISBN:** 978-1-4926-6854-6  \n\n**Summary:** This mystery novel follows the protagonist as they relive the same day eight times, each time inhabiting a different guest at the Blackheath estate. The aim is to solve the murder of Evelyn Hardcastle before the day resets. The novel blends elements of Agatha Christie-style country house mystery with a unique time-loop structure, exploring themes of perspective and identity.\n\n**Key Awards/Nominations:**\n- Costa First Novel Award (Winner)\n\n**Genre Positioning:** The novel is categorized in the mystery genre but is notable for its experimental narrative structure, placing it at the intersection of mystery and speculative fiction.\n\n### 2. Time-Loop and Body-Switching Premise\nIn *The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle*, the protagonist must navigate a complex time-loop scenario where they are forced to relive the same day repeatedly. Each time, they embody a different character present at the Blackheath estate. This unique body-switching mechanism allows the protagonist to gather information and viewpoints about the events leading to Evelyn Hardcastle's murder. Each perspective they inhabit reveals varying insights, complicating the narrative and deepening the exploration of moral responsibility and the nature of truth.\n\n### 3. Reviews and Scholarly Articles\nSeveral reviews and critical analyses discuss Turton's innovative use of the Groundhog Day structure within a murder mystery context. The recursive nature of the narrative and the diverse perspectives provided by the time-loop format have been praised as fresh and engaging, marking it as a significant contribution to contemporary mystery literature. In-depth critical overviews can often be found in major literary outlets.\n\n### 4. Turton Interviews on Influences and Writing Process\nStuart Turton has shared insights into his influences and writing process in various interviews. He discusses how his research and various literary inspirations shape his work, particularly in crafting the intricate layers of *The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle*. Interviews with him explore his motivations, thematic concerns, and the challenges he faced in structuring such a complex narrative.\n\n### Additional Resources\n1. [Wikipedia Entry on The Seven Deaths of Evelyn Hardcastle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Seven_Deaths_of_Evelyn_Hardcastle) - A comprehensive overview of the book.\n2. Critical reviews and biographies are available through various literary websites for deeper exploration of the text and its reception.\n\nThese insights should provide a solid foundation for your graduate seminar module on experimental narrative structures. If you need more specific articles or sources, please let me know!",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
  ],
